Apple today announced new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/25/apple-announces-2026-mac-mini/">M6 and M5 Pro Mac mini models</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/25/apple-announces-new-mac-studio-with-m5-ultra-chip/">M5 Max and M5 Ultra Mac Studio</a> models. We've <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/25/everything-apple-announced-today/">covered all of the announcements in-depth</a>, but wanted to highlight some interesting tidbits about the new machines.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/Apple-New-Macs-and-Polishing-Cloth.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1061010" /><br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>Price Increases</strong> - The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/mac-mini/">Mac mini</a> now starts at &#36;899, &#36;300 over the original starting price of the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/m4-mac-mini/">M4 Mac mini</a> when it launched in October 2024. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/mac-studio/">Mac Studio</a> pricing starts at &#36;2,499, &#36;500 more than the original price of the M4 Max model when it came out in March 2025.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Connectivity</strong> - Apple upgraded the new Macs with Wi-Fi 7 and Bluetooth 6, so they are on par with the connectivity standards in the latest iPhone models. Wi-Fi 7 offers faster data speeds in the 6GHz band, lower latency, and an option to connect across 2.4GHz, 5GHz, and 6GHz networks at once for reliability improvements.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Genlock</strong> - The &zwnj;Mac mini&zwnj; and &zwnj;Mac Studio&zwnj; support genlock over USB-C, so there's no need for a separate sync box. Genlock is used in multi-camera shoots and virtual production to lock timing to a shared reference signal. The Mac's display and the camera filming it are synchronized, preventing flickering and tearing from a mismatch between the display refresh rate and camera shutter. Apple previously added genlock support to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17-pro/">iPhone 17 Pro</a> models, so now an &zwnj;iPhone 17 Pro&zwnj; and one of the new Macs can work in tandem for pros who need the feature.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Ethernet</strong> - The &zwnj;Mac mini&zwnj; now starts with 2.5Gb Ethernet instead of 1Gb. There's an option to upgrade to 10Gb, which is what the &zwnj;Mac Studio&zwnj; starts with (same as the prior-generation model).</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Neural Engine</strong> - The M6 chip has an upgraded Neural Engine with two 16-core engines instead of just one. Apple says the new Neural Engine offers 2x more peak compute so AI workflows run faster.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>GPU</strong> - The M6 &zwnj;Mac mini&zwnj;'s 12-core GPU has Neural Accelerators in each core, offering up to 4x faster AI performance and 2x faster graphics than the &zwnj;M4 Mac mini&zwnj;. The &zwnj;Mac Studio&zwnj;'s M5 Ultra is also the first Ultra chip with Neural Accelerators. Peak AI compute performance is 4.3x the M3 Ultra's performance.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>SSD</strong> - &zwnj;Mac Studio&zwnj; storage is twice as fast with new SSD architecture built on PCIe Gen 6.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>SSD Pricing</strong> - As <em><a href="https://daringfireball.net/2026/08/configurations_and_pricing_for_new_mac_minis_and_mac_studios">Daring Fireball</a></em> points out, upgrading a &zwnj;Mac mini&zwnj; with a 2TB SSD costs &#36;1,000, which is more than the &#36;899 base price of the machine. Upgrading to the 4TB SSD for the M5 Pro costs &#36;1,800, which is &#36;100 over the price of the base machine.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Thunderbolt</strong> - The M6 &zwnj;Mac mini&zwnj; continues to have Thunderbolt 4, not Thunderbolt 5. The M5 Pro model does have Thunderbolt 5.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Current Max Pricing</strong> - An M5 Pro &zwnj;Mac mini&zwnj; with 18-core CPU, 64GB RAM, an 8TB SSD, and 10GbE is &#36;6,799. The M5 Ultra &zwnj;Mac Studio&zwnj; with 36-core CPU, 256GB RAM, and 16TB SSD is &#36;18,299.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>512GB RAM</strong> - You can only buy the M5 Ultra with 96GB or 256GB of RAM right now, but a 512GB option is coming in late October. Since upgrading from 96GB RAM to 256GB RAM costs &#36;4,000, the 512GB option will likely cost at least &#36;6,000. </li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Announcement Timing</strong> - This is the first time Apple has announced new Macs in August since the 27-inch <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/imac/">iMac</a> debuted in August 2020.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>macOS Golden Gate</strong> - When the new machines launch on September 22, they will likely have <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS Golden Gate</a> installed. The software update is probably going to come out the week of September 14.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
